## Context
Parent: 1229. The mechanical half of the author's checklist, as a zero-LLM
script that `/harness-doctor` (1233) runs on demand. It is a doctor's
instrument, not a guard: it never runs in the adherence command, the merge
gate or at session start, and its output is evidence for the doctor's
report, not a pass or fail.

Checks over `skills/*/SKILL.md` and `skills/*/references/*.md`:
- body line count over 150;
- fenced code blocks or heredocs over a small line threshold (the script
  belongs in `scripts/`);
- ticket numbers, merge-request numbers, dated filenames, project names;
- history phrasing (`phase N`, `since we`, `used to`, incident dates).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One script under `scripts/`, emitting findings per file and line in a
      form the doctor reads (JSON plus a short human summary)
- [ ] `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md` is the positive control: flagged on line
      count, code-block length and history phrasing
- [ ] Project-name list is data, not hardcoded in the script
- [ ] A unit test covers the script's detectors on fixtures; no test runs the
      script over the live skills, and nothing wires it into the gate
- [ ] No model call

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27)

**Premise holds.** `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md`: 235 lines; first fence lines 37-65 (27-line script); history phrasing and dated filenames at 15, 56, 63, 71, 76, 85, 88, 111. `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` states project names "cannot be caught by static grep" and greps only paths, `gh`, `github.com`: no duplication.

**Simplest path.** One `scripts/skill_text_lint.py`, globbing the files, reusing `skill_frontmatter.FRONTMATTER` to strip frontmatter and count body lines; JSON findings `{file, line, check, text}` plus a one-line summary per check; `--projects FILE` defaulting to the existing `scripts/projects.json` (8 names, no new list); argparse and logging per `rules/coding-python.md`.

**Thresholds.** Body > 150 lines. Fenced `bash`/`sh`/`python`/untagged block > 12 lines (examples run 2-6). Any `<<` heredoc inside a fence. History, case-insensitive: `\bphase \d`, `\bsince we\b`, `\bused to\b`, `\bformerly\b`, dates `20\d\d-\d\d(-\d\d)?`. Ticket/MR: `#\d{3,}`, `\b(ticket|MR|PR) \d+`. Project names word-bounded, skipping `harness` (in `projects.json`, hits constantly). False positives ("used to compute", dates in command examples, templates) are the doctor's to judge.

**Antipatterns.** No per-check plugin classes: a flat list of `(name, regex)`. No severity scale. No `--fail` flag; always exit 0.

**Criterion proposals.** (a) A project-name fixture built from a temp list file. (b) The trace-doctor positive control is a hand check by the doctor, since no test runs over live skills. (c) Fenced lines are scanned for dates too.

## Plan (raid 2026-10-27)
PLAN WARN: criterion 2 (trace-doctor flagged) cannot be a test, since no test may run over live skills. It is a hand check at verify time: run the script once on that file, expect findings for `body_lines` (235 > 150), `long_fence` (lines 37-65) and `history`; paste the output in the PR.

Actions
1. `scripts/skill_text_lint.py`: argparse CLI `skill_text_lint.py [paths...] [--root DIR] [--projects FILE]`. No paths: glob `skills/*/SKILL.md` and `skills/*/references/*.md` under `--root` (default: repo root). `--projects` defaults to `scripts/projects.json`; names come from its `name` field, `harness` skipped. Exit 0 always, no `--fail`, no model call, logging for the human summary (stderr).
2. Frontmatter stripped with `skill_frontmatter.FRONTMATTER`; line numbers stay file-absolute. Body line count = lines after the frontmatter.
3. Flat list `PATTERNS = [(name, regex)]`, case-insensitive, per line (fenced lines included):
   history_phase `\bphase \d`; history_since `\bsince we\b`; history_used_to `\bused to\b`; history_formerly `\bformerly\b`; date `20\d\d-\d\d(-\d\d)?`; ticket_ref `#\d{3,}`; ticket_word `\b(ticket|MR|PR) \d+`. Project names: one extra pattern `\b(?:n1|n2|...)\b` (re.escape) built from the list file.
4. Two structural checks, same finding shape: `body_lines` when body > 150 (one finding, line 1); `long_fence` for a fenced block (info string empty/bash/sh/python) with more than 12 content lines (finding at the opening fence line); `heredoc` for `<<` inside any fence.
5. Output on stdout: JSON `{"files": N, "findings": [{"file","line","check","text"}], "summary": {check: count}}`; one human line per check on stderr.
6. Docstring states: doctor's instrument, never a gate, false positives ("used to compute", dates in command examples) are the doctor's to judge.

FIRST failing test: `tests/test_skill_text_lint.py::test_long_fence_flags_13_lines_not_12`. Fixture (tmp_path `skills/a/SKILL.md`): frontmatter, then a bash fence of 12 `echo x` lines, then a second bash fence of 13. Assertion: findings with check `long_fence` are exactly one, at the second fence's opening line. Fails first with ModuleNotFoundError.

Further tests, each a positive and a negative near-miss (fixtures in tmp_path, `lint(root, projects_file)` called as a function, plus one CLI `subprocess` run on the fixture tree asserting exit 0 and parseable JSON):
- body_lines: 150 body lines (frontmatter extra) not flagged; 151 flagged.
- heredoc: `cat <<'EOF'` in a fence flagged; `a << b` in prose outside a fence not flagged.
- history: `phase 2` flagged, `phased rollout` not; `since we` flagged, `since weeks` not; `used to` flagged, and a documented false positive `used to compute` is also flagged (test pins it, comment says doctor judges); `formerly` flagged, `form` not.
- date: `2026-10-27` and `2026-10` flagged, `2026-1` not; one inside a fence flagged (criterion c).
- ticket_ref: `#1234` flagged, `#12` not; `ticket 1234` and `MR 7` flagged, `ticket list` not.
- projects: temp list file `[{"name":"zeta","path":"x"},{"name":"harness","path":"y"}]`: `zeta` flagged, `harness` not, `zetas` not; a second list file changes the result (criterion: names are data).
- references glob: a hit under `references/x.md` is found; a file under `notes/` is not.

Files touched: scripts/skill_text_lint.py (new), tests/test_skill_text_lint.py (new), tickets/1234-*.erg (this plan). Not touched: the adherence command, any hook, CI, other tests.

## Feasibility (raid 2026-10-27): PASS
- Import `skill_frontmatter.FRONTMATTER`; never compile a `\A---` regex. `test_frontmatter_regex_has_single_definition` fails on a second definition anywhere in the source tree.
- Positive control verified: trace-doctor is 235 lines, with a fence at 37-65 (27 content lines). It has only one history-phrase line, so date hits carry most of that check: expect `history_*` count >= 1, not many.
- `scripts/projects.json` is a list of `{name,path}` (8 entries, `harness` first), as the plan assumes. A list file is the only data source; no keys or network.
- The output wrapper `{files,findings,summary}` is the 1233 contract (1233 reads `.findings[]`). scripts/ sits outside SKILL_PATTERNS, so docstring script paths are safe.
